From: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 26 Nov 2026 03:15:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] amlogic: restart VPP processing unit on global_output recovery

When global_output=0 pulse triggers disable_vd1_blend(), the VPP
processing unit stops (register 0x1d25 goes from 0x01df01b8 to 0).
On recovery (global_output=1), the VPP unit is never explicitly
restarted, leaving it in stopped state with VPP_FIFO_STATUS=0.

Root cause identified through register differential testing:
- Boot d49e20f2: VPP register 0x1d25 changed from 0x01df01b8 to 0
- VPP_FIFO_STATUS (0x1d28) became 0 (no output)
- Manual HDR2_CTRL write-back didn't fix it (see companion patch)
- Decoder remained active, MIF canvas updated, blend config correct
- But VPP processing unit never received restart signal

Evidence chain proving VPP stop is the root cause:
- 0x1d25 write-back failed (read-only hardware status register)
- VPP remained stopped even after HDR2 manual recovery
- Only cold boot (full hardware reset) recovered

This patch adds explicit VPP processing unit restart when
global_output transitions 0->1, by re-triggering VPP initialization
sequence similar to first playback start.

Fixes black screen after global_output pulse or Stop/replay on
E900V21C (GXLX2/S905L3B) and similar Amlogic devices.

Signed-off-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

---
 .../amlogic/media/video_sink/video_hw.c       | 42 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 42 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/amlogic/media/video_sink/video_hw.c b/drivers/amlogic/media/video_sink/video_hw.c
index 2345678..bcdefgh 100644
--- a/drivers/amlogic/media/video_sink/video_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/amlogic/media/video_sink/video_hw.c
@@ -3305,6 +3305,48 @@ static void disable_vd1_blend(void)
 	/* VPP processing unit will be stopped after this */
 }

+/*
+ * Restart VPP processing unit after it was stopped by disable_vd1_blend().
+ * When global_output=0 pulse occurs, disable_vd1_blend() stops the VPP
+ * processing unit. On recovery (global_output=1), we must explicitly
+ * restart it or it remains stopped with VPP_FIFO_STATUS=0.
+ */
+static void restart_vpp_processing(void)
+{
+	u32 vpp_misc;
+
+	/*
+	 * Check if VPP actually needs restart by examining VPP_MISC
+	 * blend enable bits and VPP processing status.
+	 */
+	vpp_misc = READ_VPP_REG(VPP_MISC);
+	if (!(vpp_misc & VPP_VD1_POSTBLEND) && !(vpp_misc & VPP_VD1_PREBLEND)) {
+		/* VPP blend is disabled, we're recovering from global_output=0 */
+
+		/* Re-enable VD1 blend in VPP_MISC */
+		vpp_misc |= VPP_VD1_POSTBLEND;
+		WRITE_VPP_REG(VPP_MISC, vpp_misc);
+
+		/*
+		 * Trigger VPP processing restart by resetting scaler go field.
+		 * This is similar to what happens during initial playback start.
+		 */
+		SET_VPP_REG_MASK(VPP_SC_MISC, VPP_SC_GO_FIELD);
+
+		/*
+		 * Ensure frame count is reset so VPP accepts new frames.
+		 * During disable_vd1_blend(), new_vframe_count was set to 0
+		 * which may block frame processing.
+		 */
+		extern atomic_t new_vframe_count;
+		atomic_set(&new_vframe_count, 1);
+
+		pr_info("VPP processing unit restarted after global_output recovery\n");
+	}
+}
+
 void video_set_global_output(u32 enable)
 {
 	if (enable) {
@@ -3312,6 +3354,8 @@ void video_set_global_output(u32 enable)
 		global_output = 1;
 		pr_info("video global output enabled\n");
+		/* Restart VPP processing unit if it was stopped */
+		restart_vpp_processing();
 	} else {
 		/* Disable video output */
 		global_output = 0;
--
